From 7b2d82e89fe4ac17968838987db7056d1692a2fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:26:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] claims: every statement on the home page, the format page,
 the v1.1.0 kind pages and the RFC is a qualifier record

90 claims in docs/model/claims.json (quote + file), each with a record on its
own lines tagged claim:<id>: pass with the test or snapshot that proves it,
concern with the gap, blocker when false today (v1.1.0's meta.source list
omits copilot). One more blocker sits on RFC.md:303 for origin/main's text,
which still names v1.0.0 as the only kind; the wip text resolves it (#369).

toolpath-model reads the claim's record as its status (pass -> pinned,
concern -> partly, blocker -> false, none -> no_record) and keeps the
snapshot reading beside it; check() flags a claim with no record, and
tests/claims.rs fails from the working tree when a claim's text has no
live record covering it.
